1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:16,460
Let us pray that we love you in this place this morning.

2
00:00:16,460 --> 00:00:19,640
We praise you, Lord, and we give you all the glory, all the honor.

3
00:00:19,640 --> 00:00:21,400
Come, please do this.

4
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:25,300
Continue to be with us, but in the mercy, Lord, let us speak to our hearts.

5
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:32,620
For us, Lord, let us pray that we thank you for the glory of Jesus Christ.

6
00:00:32,620 --> 00:00:35,920
We love you, Lord, and Jesus, and we thank you. Amen.

7
00:00:55,560 --> 00:01:05,180
Let us pray, and I give you the exact proportions, because if he goes long, we agree in that time that it's possible that I go through it.

8
00:01:05,180 --> 00:01:14,860
You know, there's a million possibilities this morning, but I'm excited about this opportunity to dive into God's Word together, and it is a unique opportunity.

9
00:01:14,860 --> 00:01:32,380
We're kind of hopping into a new sermon series, mostly starting next week, and so I really just wanted to take this Sunday and take a look back at what God has done over the past year, and look forward to what God might be doing in our truth moving forward.

10
00:01:32,380 --> 00:01:40,020
I wanted to take an opportunity to test vision about what I believe and what I see God being in our truth moving forward.

11
00:01:40,020 --> 00:01:55,140
And at the same time, I recognize that there are many of you in the seats out there that have not been a part of either of us in the past, and so it's unique for you, because you're going to be hearing the story of what God did to kind of bring our churches together.

12
00:01:55,140 --> 00:02:02,680
But I think it's an important concept, as we get excited about what God might do through our churches moving forward.

13
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:16,420
I know there's people who are nearly in the room because we've been looking at the numbers, and our average attendance on Sundays as a new church is larger than if we took both of our churches' best Sundays and put them together.

14
00:02:16,420 --> 00:02:18,220
And so I know there are new people here.

15
00:02:18,220 --> 00:02:20,760
We're excited that you're here.

16
00:02:21,860 --> 00:02:41,940
And finally, at the same time, I realize that some of you in this room are going through so much right now, so much difficulty, so much pain, so much confusion, that even if you wanted to, you don't have the emotional or spiritual bandwidth to care about what we're doing as an organization.

17
00:02:41,940 --> 00:02:43,720
You're just trying to keep your head above the water.

18
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:52,660
And so, I didn't want to give this amazing, visionary, long-term future of our organization training without having some practical ramifications.

19
00:02:52,660 --> 00:03:03,020
And so, I'm going to kind of share big-picture visionary casting for our organization, and then ask them to come up and take some of those same principles and share them.

20
00:03:03,020 --> 00:03:11,580
For those of you that are like, hey, well, that's all great, wonderful, love to hear it for you all, but, like, I need some rebuilding in my own life.

21
00:03:12,340 --> 00:03:18,780
Like, we're going to talk about what it's going to look like for us to rebuild as a new church together, but I need to work on myself.

22
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:26,280
I need God to show up and do some great things in my life before I can ever think about the organization that we're a part of.

23
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:28,840
And so, that's kind of the direction for this morning.

24
00:03:28,840 --> 00:03:38,740
Now, we have a visionary message for our church as a whole, but then that outline would seem to be saying not just what our church is, but us as individuals.

25
00:03:38,740 --> 00:03:39,700
Does that make sense?

26
00:03:39,700 --> 00:03:40,820
Does that make sense?

27
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:43,620
That's the direction we have, or let them let me say yes to me.

28
00:03:43,620 --> 00:03:47,760
So, you know, that's the repeated joke, and so I don't have anything funny to say.

29
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:48,820
I'll just say that every Sunday.

30
00:03:48,820 --> 00:03:51,500
So, let me pray, and then we'll hop in.

31
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:58,380
Father, I thank you for all that you have done this past year to my church, in both of our churches.

32
00:03:58,380 --> 00:04:11,340
God, the announcement with Mike is just one microcosm of you taking the humility and faithfulness of your people and allowing them to be used far beyond anything.

33
00:04:11,340 --> 00:04:13,600
You're a God that you could ever ask and imagine.

34
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:19,740
Because you are a God that takes humble sacrifices and multiplies them.

35
00:04:19,740 --> 00:04:25,320
You're a God that takes a few rows and a couple of fifths and feeds 5,000 of them.

36
00:04:25,320 --> 00:04:32,740
So, God, we come to you today with a few levels and a couple of fifths and a speedy around us that's embarrassing.

37
00:04:32,740 --> 00:04:43,240
God, we ask that you would take our minuscule sacrifice, the little bit of skills and talents and abilities and obedience that we have to offer, and that you would multiply them.

38
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:52,860
That we would be a spiritual kingdom outpost in our city with long-term acceptance, that we would introduce more people to Jesus.

39
00:04:54,140 --> 00:04:57,060
For your glory and for our good, in Jesus' name I pray.

40
00:04:57,060 --> 00:04:57,840
Amen.

41
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:03,240
So, last month, I sat down to write what is called a pastor's report.

42
00:05:03,240 --> 00:05:08,160
And a pastor's report is something that Matt and I do every month to our board.

43
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:14,460
Just kind of a one-page seat of what God's doing, what we've been involved in throughout the month.

44
00:05:14,460 --> 00:05:18,160
We've done accountability, a little bit of kind of separating and vision casting.

45
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:30,280
And when I sat down to think about what I should write, I was thinking about where God had brought us as a church in the past and where I believed we were going to go in the future as a church.

46
00:05:30,280 --> 00:05:37,180
And God just kept drawing my money back to one of my favorite books in the Old Testament, and it's the book of Nehemiah.

47
00:05:37,180 --> 00:05:47,060
And in Nehemiah, I saw these patterns of God using Nehemiah and Israelite people to rebuild the walls of Jerusalem.

48
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:57,740
And I saw this pattern that I think really kind of is replicated in a lot of different organizations and individuals' lives when they think about rebuilding.

49
00:05:57,740 --> 00:06:07,180
Like, Nehemiah has these principles for rebuilding that I think we can use as an organization as we seek to rebuild.

50
00:06:07,180 --> 00:06:14,480
And we as individuals, we can take those same principles and use them as we think about rebuilding.

51
00:06:15,480 --> 00:06:17,540
These are principles.

52
00:06:17,540 --> 00:06:20,180
It's important that we realize these are principles and like promises.

53
00:06:20,180 --> 00:06:28,360
Because what happens oftentimes is when we flip to books of the Bible in the Old Testament or the Proverbs, wisdom literature,

54
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:32,740
oftentimes we read them as if they're promises written specifically to us.

55
00:06:32,740 --> 00:06:38,760
When in reality, they're history or principles that were written broadly.

56
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:41,680
And we try to apply them like they're promises to us.

57
00:06:41,680 --> 00:06:49,760
And so what I don't want you to hear is that if we apply these principles, that our success is going to be perfect.

58
00:06:49,760 --> 00:06:51,440
It's promised by God.

59
00:06:51,440 --> 00:06:57,340
These are just wise principles that I believe if we will put to practice as in a church,

60
00:06:57,340 --> 00:07:03,480
and if you will put them to practice in your individual lives, that God might do some things through that.

61
00:07:03,980 --> 00:07:04,620
Does that make sense?

62
00:07:04,620 --> 00:07:05,900
All right.

63
00:07:05,900 --> 00:07:10,540
So before we hop into the principles, let me give you a quick first-notes version of Nehemiah.

64
00:07:10,540 --> 00:07:14,680
This is a super condensed first-notes version because we don't have a lot of time.

65
00:07:14,680 --> 00:07:24,500
Nehemiah is one of God's chosen people at a time when God's people were far from their calling as a nation.

66
00:07:25,040 --> 00:07:29,760
They've been drawn out of the nation and put into captivity for hundreds of years,

67
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:34,360
and they were about as far away from success as they could possibly be.

68
00:07:34,360 --> 00:07:42,520
And yet, in that time, God began to move in light of some of the prophecies that he had made through his prophets.

69
00:07:42,520 --> 00:07:45,420
He said that the nation of Israel was going to be restored,

70
00:07:45,420 --> 00:07:49,340
and God began to do some miraculous things through some secular kings.

71
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:52,420
Secular kings were saying, you go back to your nation.

72
00:07:52,420 --> 00:07:57,920
Here, take money, take resources, and you go back, and you honor the things that your God has called you to do.

73
00:07:57,920 --> 00:08:04,800
God began to do miraculous things that he's used individuals throughout that story

74
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:08,420
to come alongside and to be obedient to those things.

75
00:08:08,420 --> 00:08:14,280
And so, again, in that context, it's important to realize that any time you're doing anything for God,

76
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:20,440
there's this prophecy where God's pretty much doing it miraculously showing up.

77
00:08:20,440 --> 00:08:24,000
He's moving in and through all of these opportunities,

78
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:28,460
and yet he calls us to come alongside him to partner with him in what he's doing.

79
00:08:28,460 --> 00:08:30,820
And that's what we see in the book of Ezra and Nehemiah.

80
00:08:30,820 --> 00:08:35,080
These people, God's people, come alongside what God is doing,

81
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:39,360
and they begin to reestablish the community of Israel.

82
00:08:39,360 --> 00:08:44,680
So they begin to rebuild the temple in Jerusalem, and they begin to rebuild the walls around Jerusalem.

83
00:08:44,680 --> 00:08:50,020
And Nehemiah is an individual who feels called to participate in this process.

84
00:08:50,020 --> 00:08:57,580
And also, he's going to become one of the key leaders that organizes the rebuilding of the wall.

85
00:08:57,580 --> 00:09:04,640
And it's with that context that we see these four principles lived out through Nehemiah.

86
00:09:04,640 --> 00:09:08,460
Principle number one for faithful rebuilding.

87
00:09:08,620 --> 00:09:13,240
We're going to be about rebuilding God's plan for our life.

88
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:15,940
His plan for our church faithfully.

89
00:09:15,940 --> 00:09:16,740
I would say this.

90
00:09:16,740 --> 00:09:19,000
Number one is agreeing with God.

91
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:22,120
Nehemiah chapter 1, starting in verse 8.

92
00:09:22,120 --> 00:09:28,200
Nehemiah hears that the things are not going well for Jerusalem,

93
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:30,360
and his heart is broken over, and he says this.

94
00:09:30,360 --> 00:09:31,780
He prays to God in verse 8.

95
00:09:31,780 --> 00:09:35,080
He says, please remember what you told your servants, Moses.

96
00:09:36,220 --> 00:09:39,340
If you are unfaithful to me, I will scow you among the nations.

97
00:09:39,340 --> 00:09:42,940
But if you return to me, and obey my commands, and live by them,

98
00:09:42,940 --> 00:09:46,140
then even if you are exiled to the ends of the earth,

99
00:09:46,140 --> 00:09:50,800
I will bring you back to the place that I have chosen for my name to be honored.

100
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:57,060
So Nehemiah hears that things aren't going the way that they should be going for the nation of Israel.

101
00:09:57,540 --> 00:09:59,700
And he prays to God.

102
00:09:59,700 --> 00:10:04,320
He says, God, remember what you said to your servant Moses.

103
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:09,100
You said that we would be scattered if we disobeyed, but if we return to you, you would be faithful.

104
00:10:09,100 --> 00:10:12,640
No matter how far, no matter how much we've messed up, no matter how far we've gone,

105
00:10:12,640 --> 00:10:15,260
you would bring us back to yourself.

106
00:10:15,260 --> 00:10:18,320
Nehemiah has this burden, this prayer of repentance,

107
00:10:18,320 --> 00:10:21,860
where he agrees with the promises of God, with the things of God.

108
00:10:21,920 --> 00:10:28,560
He confesses his own sin, the way that he has participated in the rebellion that led them into captivity.

109
00:10:28,560 --> 00:10:38,920
I think this principle is clearly articulated through the leadership of our churches.

110
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:45,740
Both of our churches kind of found ourselves in situations where we had to be internally associated.

111
00:10:46,440 --> 00:10:51,940
Like, we know that the mission of the church in the New Testament is the Great Commission.

112
00:10:51,940 --> 00:10:54,900
We are to go out and to make disciples of all nations.

113
00:10:54,900 --> 00:10:57,260
We are to be externally focused.

114
00:10:57,260 --> 00:11:01,340
And we both found ourselves in circumstances where we had to be internally focused.

115
00:11:01,340 --> 00:11:05,720
And our leadership said, this is necessary, but we can't stay here.

116
00:11:05,720 --> 00:11:08,680
We can't get comfortable in a place where we're internally focused.

117
00:11:08,780 --> 00:11:17,180
How can we, how can we look for ways to agree with God and find ways for God to do some miraculous things for us?

118
00:11:17,180 --> 00:11:24,380
I think it's in that process we begin to pray and God begin to move and introduce people to other people.

119
00:11:24,380 --> 00:11:29,920
And we begin to say, what if, what if we're going to be better together in a church than separate?

120
00:11:30,680 --> 00:11:34,640
And so God, because of our agreement with Him and saying, we need to be externally focused.

121
00:11:34,640 --> 00:11:37,460
Right now we're internally focused and it's not okay to stay there.

122
00:11:37,460 --> 00:11:41,980
We need to be externally focused and we begin to agree with God.

123
00:11:41,980 --> 00:11:48,140
May we as individuals, may we never lose sight of God's purposes for His church.

124
00:11:48,140 --> 00:11:53,020
May we never become comfortable just going to church.

125
00:11:53,020 --> 00:11:55,660
By doing the things that we've always done.

126
00:11:55,660 --> 00:11:57,800
This is not just as God.

127
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:05,220
When we get comfortable, when we just set boxes and go through patterns and do the things that we've always done.

128
00:12:05,220 --> 00:12:07,900
May we be externally focused.

129
00:12:07,900 --> 00:12:13,300
May we agree with the things of God, even when it calls us to obedience into things that are uncomfortable.

130
00:12:13,300 --> 00:12:15,240
The things that are difficult.

131
00:12:15,240 --> 00:12:17,420
The things that are challenging for us.

132
00:12:17,420 --> 00:12:19,100
May we be willing to be courageous.

133
00:12:19,100 --> 00:12:25,140
I love what Miles from the delegation came in this interview in that mile about the merger.

134
00:12:25,140 --> 00:12:27,400
And he said, thanks for being courageous.

135
00:12:27,400 --> 00:12:35,140
So there's a ton of churches that have opportunities like this that I know of that, you know, just be too hard.

136
00:12:35,140 --> 00:12:38,900
They'd be too difficult for them to even step out and do something that's wild.

137
00:12:38,900 --> 00:12:40,240
And you guys were courageous.

138
00:12:40,240 --> 00:12:43,480
We as a church, we've been courageous to agree with God.

139
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:50,020
And not only to agree with God, but to do the next thing, to take the first step.

140
00:12:50,020 --> 00:12:54,160
So this is, Nehemiah doesn't just agree with God.

141
00:12:54,160 --> 00:12:59,720
He doesn't just confess, protest, pray, and say, God, I want you to do the thing you said you were going to do.

142
00:12:59,720 --> 00:13:02,300
Nehemiah says, I'm going to participate in this process.

143
00:13:03,360 --> 00:13:07,440
So not only does he repent you and pray and say, God, I want you to do something miraculous.

144
00:13:07,440 --> 00:13:08,720
But he takes the first step.

145
00:13:08,720 --> 00:13:13,180
Nehemiah chapter 2, after his prayer of confession, verse 1, it says,

146
00:13:13,560 --> 00:13:28,520
Sounds like a cool job, I think, unless somebody doesn't like the king, then all of a sudden it's the worst job on the planet.

147
00:13:28,520 --> 00:13:33,420
And so, I had never before appeared sad in the king's presence.

148
00:13:33,420 --> 00:13:37,100
And so the king asked me, why are you looking so sad?

149
00:13:37,100 --> 00:13:38,640
You don't look sick to me.

150
00:13:38,640 --> 00:13:40,660
You must be deeply troubled.

151
00:13:40,760 --> 00:13:44,880
The king was very concerned if Nehemiah was sick or not, because Nehemiah had the first sip of wine.

152
00:13:44,880 --> 00:13:47,560
So, if he was sick, somebody was trying to kill him.

153
00:13:47,560 --> 00:13:48,920
He was like, I don't think you're sick.

154
00:13:48,920 --> 00:13:49,740
I think you're sad.

155
00:13:49,740 --> 00:13:54,320
And Nehemiah became terrified, and he replied, long live the king.

156
00:13:54,320 --> 00:13:55,540
How can I not be sad?

157
00:13:55,540 --> 00:14:00,560
So the city where my ancestors are buried is in ruins, and the gates have been destroyed by fire.

158
00:14:00,560 --> 00:14:03,300
And the king asked, well, how can I help you?

159
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:05,720
Listen to Nehemiah.

160
00:14:05,720 --> 00:14:07,860
He says, with a prayer to the God of heaven.

161
00:14:08,460 --> 00:14:11,620
He knew that this was going to be a difficult thing for him to do.

162
00:14:11,620 --> 00:14:14,380
He's stepping out and said, this will be a prayer to the God of heaven.

163
00:14:14,380 --> 00:14:21,580
I replied, if it pleases the king, which you are pleased with me, and so send me to Judah to rebuild the city where my ancestors are buried.

164
00:14:21,580 --> 00:14:25,840
The king and the queen sitting beside him asked, how long will you be gone?

165
00:14:25,840 --> 00:14:27,440
And when will you return?

166
00:14:27,440 --> 00:14:33,340
After I told him how long I will be gone, the king agreed to my request.

167
00:14:33,980 --> 00:14:41,100
So Nehemiah says, when he agrees with God, he confesses, he believes what God wants to do in the people of Israel.

168
00:14:41,100 --> 00:14:43,480
But then he takes the first step of asking them.

169
00:14:43,480 --> 00:14:49,200
So you agree with God is only step one, and this is often the only step that many of us ever take.

170
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:51,080
We agree with God.

171
00:14:51,080 --> 00:14:54,200
We confess and repent, and then we do nothing about it.

172
00:14:54,200 --> 00:14:56,060
We get complacent.

173
00:14:56,620 --> 00:15:00,660
He says, godly obedience is far more difficult than godly agreement.

174
00:15:00,660 --> 00:15:12,320
I wonder if some of the most fruitful mainstreams that God's ever called us to plant or to start died between agreeing and taking the first step of asking.

175
00:15:12,320 --> 00:15:18,960
I wonder how many times God's called us as an organization, as an individual, into obedience.

176
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:27,680
And so we agreed with him, and we knew that he wanted us to do something in and through us, that he wanted us to ease our laws and our faith, the little sacrifice that we have.

177
00:15:27,680 --> 00:15:29,780
And then we agreed with him, and then we got comfortable.

178
00:15:29,780 --> 00:15:32,340
We didn't do anything about it.

179
00:15:32,340 --> 00:15:40,740
Mercy's parents were here over Christmas, and we were reflecting on stories that a child had as we're about to have our first.

180
00:15:40,740 --> 00:15:44,820
We're trying to imagine what a child might be like, based on the music here and the music here.

181
00:15:45,880 --> 00:15:46,880
Yes, good luck.

182
00:15:46,880 --> 00:15:48,260
Really, really good luck.

183
00:15:48,260 --> 00:15:55,660
And her mom said, you know, Marissa was, she would say no all day long, regardless of what she was actually doing.

184
00:15:55,660 --> 00:16:02,440
The middle child, the classic middle child, she would yes me to death, but they never actually do it.

185
00:16:02,440 --> 00:16:06,680
And so she had the appearance of being this, like, awesome child, right?

186
00:16:06,680 --> 00:16:08,680
She was always, yes, mom, yes, mom, yes, mom.

187
00:16:08,680 --> 00:16:14,880
But if she actually paid attention to her solace and she didn't do anything about it, how often are we as Christians like that?

188
00:16:14,940 --> 00:16:16,600
Yes, God, yes, God, yes, God.

189
00:16:16,600 --> 00:16:27,900
But then when it takes the time to actually step out and say, God, how often are we that person that just yes is God to them, but doesn't do anything about it?

190
00:16:27,900 --> 00:16:31,220
Step one is to agree with God.

191
00:16:31,220 --> 00:16:37,060
Step two is to take us to, and I believe our church is merging as a result of the first two steps in this process.

192
00:16:37,060 --> 00:16:43,660
Both of our churches, we were discontent with being inward focused, and our leadership led us to take difficult steps.

193
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:45,620
And we've taken more than one.

194
00:16:45,620 --> 00:16:53,100
We've taken a few really difficult steps, and it's because of your humility and your faithfulness and your willingness to listen to God and step out and take action,

195
00:16:53,100 --> 00:16:57,480
even if you weren't 100% sure if it was going to lead to the things that you wanted it to lead to.

196
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:07,880
And we've seen God move in these principles of rebuilding, and we've agreed that God was taking steps of action, and it's led to a fruitful new church beginning.

197
00:17:07,880 --> 00:17:18,700
And we continue to be a church full of individuals who aren't willing to just be comfortable to just agree with God, but is that we take action courageously.

198
00:17:19,360 --> 00:17:21,080
And we're sensing God leading us.

199
00:17:21,080 --> 00:17:31,880
This is an excellent foundation for the church to be worked on individuals, and we pray like it depends on God, and we ask like it depends on others.

200
00:17:31,880 --> 00:17:35,360
Not just to agree with God, but to take steps of action.

201
00:17:35,360 --> 00:17:39,820
And the third principle is to make good plans.

202
00:17:40,820 --> 00:17:43,160
Nehemiah doesn't just take action, but he thinks about it.

